# Cloudflare Pages routing — Bennett Studio.
#
# There is deliberately NO `/*` catch-all here. How Pages actually behaves,
# verified against `wrangler pages dev`:
#
#   1. Valid _redirects rules are evaluated BEFORE static assets. A rule like
#      `/*  /some-shell  200` therefore wins over every prerendered file and
#      serves that one shell for the entire site. Do not add one.
#
#   2. The classic SPA line `/*  /index.html  200` is REJECTED by Pages as a
#      self-referential loop ("Infinite loop detected in this rule and has been
#      ignored") because Pages canonicalises /index.html back to /. It was in
#      this file for months and never did anything.
#
#   3. Deep links work regardless: Pages natively falls back to index.html for
#      any path that matches no asset, as long as no 404.html exists. That —
#      not rule 2 — is what has always served /marginprint and friends, and it
#      is why scripts/prerender.mjs writes flat <route>.html files that Pages
#      can match directly.
#
# So the only rule needed is the alias below. /api/* Pages Functions are
# evaluated before any of this.
/makerbooks    /maker-books    301
